# Backend Django conventions

- Domain models: prefer `UUIDModel` + `TimeStampedModel` from `apps.core.models`; keep explicit `db_table` where existing models use it.
- Put logic in the owning app under `backend/apps/<app>/`. Register routes in that app’s `urls.py`; only add prefixes in `config/urls.py` for new top-level APIs.
- Prefer `ModelViewSet` + router for CRUD; function views for aggregates (analytics pattern).
- Permissions + queryset scoping required — see `docs/agent-kb/permissions.md`.
- Validate UUID/date query params before filtering.
- Model changes: skill `django-migrate`. New behavior: skill `write-tests` under `apps/<app>/tests/`.
- Sync protocol: read `docs/agent-kb/offline-sync.md` before editing `expenses/sync_views.py`.
